---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Boundary Survey Adelaide, Land Surveying | Torrens Survey Co"
  description="Boundary survey and land surveying in Adelaide and the Adelaide Hills. Get introduced to an independent Licensed Surveyor. Call now on (08) 5550 3814."
  canonical="https://torrenssurveyco.com/"
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@type": ["ProfessionalService", "LocalBusiness"], "@id": "https://torrenssurveyco.com/#organization", "name": "Torrens Survey Co", "url": "https://torrenssurveyco.com", "logo": {"@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://torrenssurveyco.com/images/og-image.webp"}, "priceRange": "$$", "telephone": "(08) 5550 3814", "email": "info@torrenssurveyco.com", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "addressLocality": "Adelaide", "addressRegion": "SA", "addressCountry": "AU"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": -34.9285, "longitude": 138.6007}, "areaServed": [{"@type": "City", "name": "Adelaide", "addressRegion": "SA"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Adelaide Hills & Mount Barker", "addressRegion": "SA"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Northern Adelaide", "addressRegion": "SA"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Southern Adelaide", "addressRegion": "SA"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Eastern Suburbs", "addressRegion": "SA"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Western Suburbs", "addressRegion": "SA"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Inner Adelaide", "addressRegion": "SA"}], "@context": "https://schema.org", "description": "Boundary survey and land surveying in Adelaide and the Adelaide Hills. Get introduced to an independent Licensed Surveyor. Call now on (08) 5550 3814.", "image": "https://torrenssurveyco.com/images/og-image.webp", "hasOfferCatalog": {"@type": "OfferCatalog", "name": "Land Surveying Services", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Boundary Surveys & Re-Pegging"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Feature & Level Surveys"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Land Division Surveys"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Identification Surveys"}}]}}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebSite", "@id": "https://torrenssurveyco.com/#website", "url": "https://torrenssurveyco.com", "name": "Torrens Survey Co", "publisher": {"@id": "https://torrenssurveyco.com/#organization"}}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need a boundary survey, or a different kind of survey?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It depends on the problem. A boundary survey (also called an identification survey or re-pegging) is for when you need the legal boundary marked, for example because of a fence dispute, a build close to the line or a purchase. A feature and level survey records the existing ground levels and features so a designer can draw plans. A land division survey is part of splitting a block. If you're not sure, call (08) 5550 3814 and describe the situation, and we will point you to the right one."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Who is allowed to do a boundary survey in South Australia?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The Surveyors Board of South Australia says that in South Australia, only licensed surveyors can undertake a boundary survey or place a survey mark that defines a property boundary. Torrens Survey Co isn't one of them: it's an advertising and introduction service and holds no surveying licence. Check any surveyor's licence with the Registrar at the Surveyors Board (registrar@isasa.org.au or (08) 8212 0343) before you agree to work."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How much does a boundary survey or land survey cost in Adelaide, and how is the job scoped?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Surveyors quote each job, and the price depends on the block, the evidence on site and the type of survey. None of the Adelaide firms we checked publishes a price for a boundary or feature survey, so this site doesn't either. The one sourced figure is a whole-of-project estimate for a standard one-into-two land division in metropolitan Adelaide, from one Adelaide surveying firm's published guide (May 2025): 'in the order of $30,000 – $34,000', with GST treatment not stated. That covers government fees, conveyancing and other costs as well as the surveyor, so it's not a survey price. Ask the surveyor for the scope in writing: what's measured, what you receive and what's not included. Our cost page sets out what is and isn't sourced."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How quickly can I get a survey done?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "We don't publish a lead time. We have no sourced figure for one, and it would be a guess. How soon a surveyor can start depends on their workload and the type of survey, so ask for a start date and a delivery date when they quote. A land division has approvals on top of the survey, and Land Services SA says the division of land can take many months, sometimes even years. If your timing matters, say so when you call (08) 5550 3814."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "My neighbour and I disagree about where the fence should go. What now?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "SA Government says the boundary can only be determined by a licensed surveyor, and a fence line doesn't show the legal boundary. Under the Fences Act 1975, the cost of a survey reasonably required for the fencing work can be included as a fencing cost, though your neighbour may object and a Magistrate would then decide. A neighbour has 30 days to respond to a fencing notice. By law you can't move or remove a survey mark, and for the dispute itself, talk to the Legal Services Commission, Community Mediation Services or a solicitor."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I split my block, and where does the survey fit?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "We can't tell you whether a division will be approved. That depends on your zone, the overlays and the council, so a preliminary enquiry at the council is the first step, and this site doesn't publish minimum block sizes. Land Services SA strongly recommends using a professional licensed surveyor and a conveyancer or solicitor to work out the planning requirements, draft the plans and lodge the paperwork. Our land division page and the blog on how to subdivide land in South Australia cover the steps in order."}}]}</script>
<style is:global>
  .rich p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: #555; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .rich ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .rich li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: #555; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .rich strong { color: #2B3A44; }
  .rich a { color: #1E6F63; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .rich a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
</Fragment>

<!-- HERO -->
<section style="position:relative;min-height:560px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;overflow:hidden;">
  <img src="/images/hero-panorama.webp" alt="Adelaide landscape" width="2000" height="950" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
  <div style="position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(10,61,92,0.55) 0%, rgba(10,61,92,0.25) 55%, rgba(10,61,92,0.45) 100%);"></div>
  <div style="position:relative;max-width:880px;padding:96px 24px 130px;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:18px;padding:7px 18px;border-radius:2px;font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.14);color:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.35);backdrop-filter:blur(3px);">Boundary · Contour · Subdivision · Adelaide</span>
    <h1 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-weight:700;color:#fff;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.015em;font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,58px);margin:0 0 18px;text-shadow:0 2px 24px rgba(10,61,92,0.45);">Boundary Survey and Land Surveying in Adelaide and the Adelaide Hills</h1>
    <p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.92);max-width:640px;margin:0 auto 30px;text-shadow:0 1px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.5);">Torrens Survey Co is an advertising and introduction service: we put Adelaide property owners in touch with an independent Licensed Surveyor, who quotes and contracts with you directly. Call (08) 5550 3814 or send the form, tell us what's going on with your block, and we'll help you work out which survey you need before anyone sends a quote.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <a href="tel:+61855503814" class="btn-green" style="font-size:15px;padding:16px 38px;">Call Now — (08) 5550 3814</a>
      <a href="/#contact" class="btn-white-outline" style="font-size:15px;">Get a Written Quote</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <svg class="swoosh" style="position:absolute;bottom:0;left:0;" viewBox="0 0 1440 70" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0,70 C360,10 1080,10 1440,70 L1440,70 L0,70 Z" fill="#ffffff"/></svg>
</section>

<!-- INTRO -->
<section style="padding:84px 24px 64px;background:#fff;">
  <div class="intro-grid" style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.9fr 1.1fr;gap:64px;align-items:center;">
    <div style="position:relative;">
      <div style="border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 24px 56px rgba(10,61,92,0.22);aspect-ratio:1/1;">
        <img src="/images/about.webp" alt="Torrens Survey Co service crew" width="1024" height="1024" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      <div style="position:absolute;bottom:-18px;right:-14px;background:#1E6F63;color:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:14px 22px;box-shadow:0 10px 26px rgba(47,163,77,0.4);">
        <p style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;margin:0;line-height:1;">By law</p>
        <p style="font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;margin:4px 0 0;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;">Only Licensed Surveyors peg boundaries</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="kicker">Adelaide and the Adelaide Hills</span>
      <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,40px);margin:0 0 18px;">Find out which survey you need before you pay for one</h2>
      <div class="rich"><p>Torrens Survey Co is an advertising and introduction service for Adelaide property owners. It's not a surveying firm and holds no surveying licence. When you need a boundary survey or other land surveying done, we introduce you to an independent Licensed Surveyor, who quotes and contracts with you directly.</p><p>Most enquiries come down to one of five situations: a fence going up or coming down, a designer or council asking for a <a href="/feature-and-level-surveys/">feature and level survey</a>, a block someone wants to <a href="/land-division-surveys/">divide</a>, a purchase where the house, shed and fences need checking against the title, or pegs that have gone missing. If you're not sure which applies, read <a href="/blog/what-does-a-land-surveyor-do/">what a land surveyor does</a> or <a href="/blog/licensed-surveyor-vs-registered-surveyor-sa/">the difference between licensed and registered surveyors in South Australia</a>, or just ring.</p></div>
      <a href="/about/" class="btn-blue" style="margin-top:10px;">More About Us</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .intro-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; gap: 44px !important; } }
</style>

<!-- TILES -->
<section id="services" style="padding:72px 24px 84px;background:#EEF3F1;">
  <div style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
    <span class="kicker">Where people usually start</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,40px);margin:0 0 40px;">Which of these sounds like your block?</h2>
    <div class="tile-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:22px;">
      <a href="/boundary-surveys/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/service-1.webp" alt="Timber stake with pink survey ribbon beside a Colorbond fence on an Adelaide suburban block" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;padding:14px 12px;">The pegs are gone and the boundary is a guess</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/feature-and-level-surveys/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/service-2.webp" alt="Survey instrument on a tripod in a backyard in front of a stone Adelaide house" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;padding:14px 12px;">A designer or builder wants levels before drawing plans</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/land-division-surveys/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/service-3.webp" alt="Aerial view of a long narrow allotment between older houses with a jacaranda in bloom" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;padding:14px 12px;">Thinking about splitting the block in two</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/identification-surveys/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/service-4.webp" alt="Modern single-storey house on an Adelaide street with Colorbond side fences" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;padding:14px 12px;">Buying, and want the house and fences checked against the title</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/boundary-fence-dispute-survey-sa/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/tile-1.webp" alt="Weathered timber post and rail fence beside a street with a stone villa behind it" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;padding:14px 12px;">A neighbour disagrees about where the fence should go</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/feature-survey-development-application-sa/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/tile-2.webp" alt="Rolled house plans and a coffee mug on a timber table in a backyard" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;padding:14px 12px;">Council wants a survey before your plans can go in</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/survey-pegs-missing/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/tile-3.webp" alt="Round metal survey mark cover set into a footpath" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;padding:14px 12px;">A survey mark in the ground, or none at all</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/how-to-find-property-boundaries-sa/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(10,61,92,0.1);">
        <img src="/images/tile-4.webp" alt="Backyard with a shed, clothesline and Colorbond fences and a house behind" width="700" height="560" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1.25/1;object-fit:cover;display:block;" loading="lazy">
        <span style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;padding:14px 12px;">Not sure where your boundary actually is</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  @media (max-width: 1000px) { .tile-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr) !important; } }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .tile-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; } }
</style>

<!-- SERVICE CARDS -->
<section style="padding:0 24px 80px;background:#EEF3F1;">
  <div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <div class="svc-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <a href="/boundary-surveys/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DFD4;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 10px;">Boundary Surveys & Re-Pegging</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">For a fence going up or coming down, a build close to the line, or pegs that have gone missing. In South Australia, only licensed surveyors can undertake a boundary survey or place a survey mark that defines a property boundary (Surveyors Board SA).</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#1E6F63;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/feature-and-level-surveys/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DFD4;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 10px;">Feature & Level Surveys</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">The usual way to get the existing levels and boundary offsets a site plan has to show, for an extension, a new home or a sloping block. Designers, builders and councils often ask for one before plans can go in.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#1E6F63;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/land-division-surveys/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DFD4;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 10px;">Land Division Surveys</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Torrens or community title, the surveyor prepares and lodges the plan alongside the planning, conveyancing and Land Services SA steps. Land Services SA says a division can take many months, sometimes even years.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#1E6F63;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/identification-surveys/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DFD4;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 10px;">Identification Surveys</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Buying or selling, and want to know the house, shed and fences sit inside the title? An identification survey is a cadastral survey of the existing boundaries, and the Surveyors Board says to be aware of any encroachments involving neighbouring properties.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#1E6F63;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  @media (max-width: 1000px) { .svc-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr) !important; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .svc-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; } }
</style>

<!-- WHY -->
<section style="padding:84px 24px;background:#fff;">
  <div class="why-grid" style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 0.9fr;gap:64px;align-items:center;">
    <div>
      <span class="kicker">What Makes Us Different</span>
      <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,40px);margin:0 0 28px;">Plain answers before anyone sends you a quote</h2>
      <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px;">
          <li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1E6F63" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px;"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            <div>
              <p style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 4px;">We say what we are</p>
              <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Torrens Survey Co is an advertising service, not a surveying firm, and it holds no surveying licence. The independent Licensed Surveyor quotes and contracts with you directly.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1E6F63" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px;"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            <div>
              <p style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 4px;">A licence you can check yourself</p>
              <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">The Surveyors Board of South Australia keeps a public register, and its Registrar can confirm a licence on (08) 8212 0343 or registrar@isasa.org.au. Checking before you agree to anything is the Board's own advice.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1E6F63" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px;"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            <div>
              <p style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 4px;">No made-up prices</p>
              <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">None of the Adelaide surveying firms we checked publishes a price for a boundary or feature survey, so we don't print one either. The cost page sets out the few figures that are sourced, and says where they come from.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1E6F63" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px;"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            <div>
              <p style="font-family:'Instrument Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:#111418;margin:0 0 4px;">The question comes before the sale</p>
              <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Plenty of owners ring without knowing whether they need a boundary, identification or feature survey. We talk that through first, even if it means you're not ready to book anything yet.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
